  "description": "WESSOF crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group C 2 2 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C59 H74 Gd4 N12 O23,2(C1 H4 O1),C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.917-3.960 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.91-112.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4L4(CO3)(acac)2(CH3OH)4]·2CH3OH·CH2Cl2.",
